@* HelpReadingReviewPage: help topic "Reading a review" at "/help/reading-a-review". Static text and screenshots. *@
@page "/help/reading-a-review"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="reading-a-review">
    <section class="card">
        <p>Choose a file in the review to read it. When the review has a baseline, a file opens on the
            <strong>Diff</strong> view: the earlier version on the left and the new version on the right, with
            removed lines in red and added lines in green. <strong>Head</strong> shows the new version and
            <strong>Baseline</strong> the earlier one.</p>
        <figure class="help-figure">
            <img class="help-shot" src="/help/reading-a-review-1.png" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Diff view of a file: the baseline on the left and the head on the right, removed lines in red and added lines in green, with a + button that appears when you point at a line." />
            <figcaption>The Diff view.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Each file is marked <strong>Added</strong>, <strong>Modified</strong> or <strong>Deleted</strong>. An added
            file has no Baseline view and a deleted file has no Head view.</p>
        <p>Unchanged lines far from a change are folded away; press a <strong>Show N unchanged lines</strong> button to
            see them.</p>
        <p>If you hold a reviewer slot you own a ballot: answer the checks in your own ballot, submit it, then sign.
            The review concludes when every slot has signed the same, current record.</p>
        <p>A concluded (approved or rejected) review is locked, so the <strong>+</strong> buttons and the comment forms
            are disabled. You can still read every file and diff. If you hold a slot of the review, you created it, or you
            are an administrator of the project or a system administrator,
            the <strong>Review conclusion</strong> card lets you write the reasons for the outcome while the review is
            not locked; a rejected review needs them before it can be signed. See
            <a href="/help/reviewers-and-signing">Reviewers and signing</a>.</p>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
